// EulerConvention argument-slot gate — reject fixture (task #6082).
//
// A String convention must be a COMPILE-TIME diagnostic, not a silent Undef at
// eval. Task #6082 removed the raw lowercase-string convention path from both
// Euler builtins; without a registered argument slot the removal is invisible
// to the user until the value quietly evaluates to Undef.
//
// Exactly TWO Errors are expected, both DiagnosticCode::ArgTypeMismatch — one
// per String convention below. Anti-cascade: no UnresolvedType or other
// type-cascade noise. Both calls are otherwise well-formed (correct arity,
// correct order, valid angles), so the convention slot is the only thing that
// can be wrong.
//
// "XYZ" and "xyz" cover both spellings the removed path used to discriminate:
// it accepted lowercase and silently rejected uppercase. Neither is a
// convention any more.

structure def EulerArgReject {
    let q      = orient_euler("xyz", 0.1, 0.2, 0.3)
    let angles = orient_to_euler(orient_identity(), "XYZ")
}
